    ✔ send binds allowlisted values only: one queued row per channel, a job per row in the same transaction, no address, no text (31.751839ms)
    ✔ free text, unknown names, a service or clinician field, bad links and condition-revealing location names never reach a notification (TC-NT-06) (12.546527ms)
    ✔ dedupe keys prevent double sends: a repeat creates nothing and queues nothing, also under concurrency (137.598912ms)
    ✔ a rolled-back business transaction leaves no notification and no job; a delayed send waits for send_after (27.737746ms)
    ✔ cancel by dedupe-key prefix cancels queued rows of that resource only; sent rows are final (87.660152ms)
    ✔ in-app notices: a patient lists only their own sent notices and marks them read once (21.573608ms)
  ✔ send, dedupe, cancel (22.13, 24, BR-08) (1012.116332ms)
  ▶ row-level security and grants
